# Product decisions

When the user chooses product behavior — prices, item ids, lap count, stipend, climb grade, audio asset ids, Studio place, kart rules, shop open states — record it **in that turn**.

1. Add a new `##` entry at the top of [`docs/DECISIONS.md`](docs/DECISIONS.md) (below the intro):

```markdown
## YYYY-MM-DD — short title
Decided: …
Why: …
Supersedes: … (or none)
```

2. If current law changed, patch the **Rules** section of [`docs/ROADMAP.md`](docs/ROADMAP.md) in the same turn so it matches [`ReplicatedStorage/Constants.luau`](ReplicatedStorage/Constants.luau).
3. Do **not** rewrite [`docs/v2/`](docs/v2/) phase catalogs for a tunable change. Those stay historical; ROADMAP Rules is what is true now.

Skip when the ask is review-only (no edits). Skip pure implementation with no new product call.
